current_companion_rotation_revocation_state_2026_08_24:
  authority: Remote-exact commit `6537c6070ecd109c65791493864d8bd90ac8971d`, tree `fc988afd8d9c21d13ca6a90b6abe7194e13afc6e`, implements status, rotation, exact old-commit replay, and revocation under sole corrected profile `/2`; it does not revise registration authority or read profile JSON at runtime.
  state: One 120-second pending rotation is exact-body idempotent and conflicts otherwise. Old-key authentication plus candidate-new-key proof advances at most through epoch 64, resets sequence/key age, preserves absolute expiry, and retains a 30-second exact-response replay only. Revocation proves its response before erasure. Process-lifetime revoked tombstones remain bounded by fail-closed 4,096-record admission.
  lease: Normal leases own one authenticated sequence, one private key copy, and one in-flight reservation through explicit open/executing/finished states. Failed route work reopens for one proven error; concurrent disposal cannot strand the reservation. Exact old-commit replay leases own no key, sequence, or reservation and cannot execute another route.
  evidence: Architecture `docs/architecture/2026-08-24-companion-rotation-revocation-state.md`; bytes=15746; sha256=821cfc368088d1ad8eb7f8410e0d40b9469dd2b00f289567bf10662623327542. Managed=189/189-zero-skips; Companion=71/71; browser/oracle=8/8; focused=59/59; Release warnings/errors=0; format clean. Complete Node=1173-pass/15-fail/1-skip across 1189 with private-log SHA256 0a65f69297247eae1ab4a97842c0055499469602c31fd9ddbb7d06afa50e7d74.
  boundary_and_next: No listener, browser, transfer, model, publication, deployment, MemoryEndpoints, or campaign claim follows. Implement strict numeric-loopback Kestrel and raw-socket tests next, then the memory-only browser client. Six full-gate root classes remain and prohibit deployment; counters stay zero.
current_companion_installation_pairing_session_state_2026_08_24:
  authority: Remote-exact commit `66248fd95443b5cdeac5936502a33d4488fcc235`, tree `a7ea0d31a2d0901f58994463f58825e717d7fa90`, implements the installation, pairing, and session state portion of corrected profile `/2`; it does not revise registration authority or read registration JSON at runtime.
  installation: Canonical create-only two-field installation bytes preserve one 16-byte durable ID and generate one 16-byte process ID per open. Windows root authority is protected current-user-plus-SYSTEM ACL and current-user ownership; Linux authority is root 0700, record 0600, and statx UID equal to geteuid. Missing record in a nonempty root, malformed bytes, reparse, owner, or permission drift reject without migration or repair.
  state: Explicit TRLC1 issuance owns a 300-second memory-only secret. Pairing has four pending claims, 30-second pending lifetime, 8/minute begin and complete limits, exact begin and 60-second complete replay, first-valid atomic consumption, and exactly one winner across races. Sessions are memory-only, max four, 28,800-second absolute, 900-second idle/key epoch, 600/minute, exact-next sequence, one in flight, commit-after-proof-before-handler, and proven exact-body responses with explicit key clearing.
  wire: Pairing begin/complete requests and responses have one canonical UTF-8 representation with exact member order, no final LF, and reencode equality. Whitespace, reordered, unknown, duplicate, escaped, malformed, wrong-type, and noncanonical variants reject.
  evidence: Architecture `docs/architecture/2026-08-24-companion-installation-pairing-session-state.md`; bytes=12834; sha256=2669c904cfdaf457815e806c4368e3fda07c42d3dcd6242f401cc2059b224fe2. Managed 180/180, browser/oracle 8/8, focused registration/vector/ADR 59/59, Release zero warnings, format clean. Linux behavior is compiled but not hardware-executed.
