current_companion_source_conversion_reconciliation_2026_08_24:
  authority: Output-free registration `af7857bbc4afa122d8013f2952b2944b53b6e3d2`, machine SHA256 `087038104f63d6e78373691034aaf586de803059d68c47a12acc2140bf3ac971`, architecture SHA256 `c4fe01d64a65c51e8803ae4b16bc18bfd52b868faaadf5e4003f4f40b362a180`, and remote-exact implementation `87a0fc1c799f5359b44e3e5bdcb35b2d3500f22c`, tree `5327e22727b7fc3ac7dbb8c67b7f92f2bbc418a2`, are the sole current source-conversion reconciliation authority.
  durable_contract: Companion operation schema is exactly `tinyrustlm.companion.operation.v2`; operation.v1 is rejected without migration. Before source Converting, the owner writes a canonical create-only `tinyrustlm.companion.source-conversion-intent.v1` record, reopens and validates exact canonical UTF-8/LF bytes, and binds its SHA256 into every source-branch Converting and terminal journal record. Durable verified composition and live process observation are separate schemas, so recovery never requires stdout, elapsed time, PID, or an extant process.
  reconciliation: `InspectCompositionTerminal` is read-only and classifies the bounded direct terminal root as Pending, exact Pass, exact native Rejection, or Invalid. `ReconcileTerminal` applies only to intent-bound Source Converting/VerifyingComposition. Pending performs no journal write and launches, adopts, retries, or kills nothing. Exact Pass advances to Available; exact Rejection advances to Rejected; collisions, malformed evidence, inventory drift, source/tool/profile drift, and policy violations reject with bounded stable errors. Terminal records remain immutable, and known live validation failures cannot be laundered through later durable pass bytes.
  cancellation_and_start_failure: Pre-cancelled execution never starts the converter or creates output and records Cancelled with the bound intent. Cancellation after owned process-tree termination gives durable pass precedence, then native rejection, then Cancelled only while terminal evidence remains Pending. OS process-start failure becomes typed `converter-process-start`; it cannot strand an untyped Converting operation.
  verification: Core 80/80, Companion 45/45, package 38/38, complete managed solution 163/163 with zero skips, and reconciliation preregistration 12/12 pass. Formatting, warnings-as-errors build, 49-entry public API baseline, diff hygiene, secret/path scans, and frozen goal identity pass. Clean source `87a0fc1` produced an external create-only win-x64 package audit at SHA256 `b9c11d61c0957597331823024d6e309865ff70fb7ef92035e2fad61451bdf231` and manifest SHA256 `228af1b0d0a6397e40e94d2df380328da819a7f89107719ce2991ba9b8d8e513`, all defect counts zero.
